data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** Cas9 nuclease, guided by a synthetic gRNA, cuts DNA at a chosen site [1]. Programmable molecules create double-strand breaks that allow insertion, deletion, modification, or replacement of DNA [3].\n\n- **Biological origin:** CRISPR draws on bacterial antiviral defense, where sequences derived from bacteriophage DNA help detect and destroy similar phages in later infections [1][2].\n\n- **Therapeutic hype outpaces evidence:** A Hacker News post links to NPR on treating a broad range of diseases [4]. The HIV result is from cell culture only, not patients [5]."}

